home/home.nix-288-  # Claude Code writes ~/.claude/settings.json itself: /effort, /model and
home/home.nix-289-  # /config save defaults there, and an "always allow" answer appends to
home/home.nix-290-  # permissions.allow. Each write is staged as a sibling temp file, so a
home/home.nix-291-  # home.file symlink into the store fails the whole command with EROFS
home/home.nix-292-  # ("Failed to set effort level: ... EROFS: read-only file system"). Install a
home/home.nix-293-  # real, writable copy instead and merge this repo's keys over whatever Claude
home/home.nix-294-  # Code has accumulated: the pins below win, its own keys survive. A key
home/home.nix-295-  # dropped from config/claude/settings.json lingers in the copy until it is
